1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,700
How to Read Faster Without Losing Comprehension.

2
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:10,725
True speed reading — absorbing thousands of words per minute with full comprehension — is not biologically possible.

3
00:00:10,725 --> 00:00:14,325
The eye can only focus on a narrow area at a time.

4
00:00:14,325 --> 00:00:17,700
However, reading can be made more efficient.

5
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:24,062
Reducing subvocalization, the habit of silently pronouncing each word, increases pace.

6
00:00:24,062 --> 00:00:31,425
Previewing material before reading — scanning headings, first sentences, and summaries — gives the brain a framework.

7
00:00:31,425 --> 00:00:40,187
Adjusting reading speed to material difficulty: skimming familiar content and slowing down for complex passages yields better comprehension overall.

